restore.description:
Old: {old}

New: {new}

Journal status: {status}

Restores original IDs and settings for both bulbs, including enabled state. Later edits to those settings are overwritten. History and external changes are not restored.

For ZHA copying, newly added bindings and memberships are also removed. Entries present before replacement are preserved. ZHA and the affected devices must be available.

confirm_zha.description:
**{old} → {archived}** (name: {name}_OLD, disabled).

**{new} → {old}** (name: {name}). Area ID: {area}. Area, labels, aliases and custom icon are copied.

**Resolve before replacing:** {blockers}

**Different light capabilities:** {capabilities} (`capabilities` means different color/dimming/effect support). Review scenes.

Take a HA backup. References to the original entity ID will target the new bulb. History is not migrated. Clean up references to the new bulb’s previous ID manually. external systems and dynamic templates cannot be verified here. Hardware device IDs and unique IDs stay unchanged. Pause affected automations during replacement; state changes will occur.

**ZHA bindings to copy:**
{zha_bindings}

**Zigbee groups:** {zha_groups}

**Unread / incomplete discovery:**
{zha_missing}

**Incompatible bindings (block copying):**
{zha_blockers}

Original bindings and memberships are retained. Existing bindings on the new bulb are preserved. New entries are read back to verify success. Undo removes only entries added by the wizard. Physical controls may affect both bulbs until the old one is disconnected. On-device Zigbee scenes and reporting configuration are not copied.
